  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: All four completed experiments use avgpool aggregation with multiprofile, and the current best (config_002, acc=0.629) combines pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat fusion. We have no data on whether the aggregation method (how multiple profiles are combined) meaningfully affects performance. Question: config_024 is a clean single-variable change from config_002, swapping only avgpool → transformer aggregation while keeping pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, and concat fixed. This isolates whether a learned, attention-based aggregation of profiles can outperform uniform averaging. Why this is the best next experiment: With multiprofile data, the aggregation step is a fundamental architectural choice that directly governs how profile-level information is integrated. Transformer aggregation could capture non-uniform profile importance that avgpool cannot. Testing this on the current best configuration (config_002) gives the highest information value: if it helps, we identify a compounding architectural improvement; if it doesn't, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting questions. It avoids changing multiple variables simultaneously and builds directly on the strongest existing evidence."
}

